5d46-b51c-37977a6efa1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-109390" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe matrix above has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=-3.$ Find a Jordan canonical form of the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given a $3\\times 3$ matrix that has precisely $3$ distinct eigenvalues. \n\nTherefore, $A$ is diagonalizable, and its Jordan canonical form is\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(1)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(-3)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The Jordan canonical form is unique up to the order of the Jordan blocks."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162303 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "affc4199-909a-56da-bf79-c32b2a7958f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159021} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ea3944-2a08-507e-a50d-3402518c4719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159022} {:answer/id #uuid "e8917add-f461-55f8-858a-8f2429249c81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159023} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8ebaa2-0ce9-528e-a426-757d6f1834eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159024} {:answer/id #uuid "09b0c263-bcc4-5b5e-81f1-699217d90c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159025}] :answer-field/id #uuid "59a0f29c-d8a7-56e9-bc69-08900d50d822" :answer-field/key "selection"